+/// \file
+/// Support for register-contract functions: pre-encoded code packaged as an IR
+/// function whose interface is declared by the function itself instead of by
+/// the calling convention.
+///
+/// A contract function carries
+///   "amdgpu-contract"="<name>"                       the contract name,
+///   "amdgpu-contract-clobber"="s[2:23],v[4:511],scc" every register it writes,
+/// and every parameter carries "amdgpu-reg"="<reg>" naming the physical
+/// register the value is passed in. Its body is a single basic block made of
+/// argument conversions, exactly one inline asm call that binds each parameter
+/// to its register and clobbers a subset of the declared footprint, and a ret.
+///
+/// AMDGPUExpandContractCalls (IR) checks the contract and expands every call
+/// in place, so a call costs nothing beyond moving arguments into their
+/// registers: no stack, no saved registers and no s_swap_pc. A call site may be
+/// preceded by a marker `call void asm sideeffect ";@amdgpu-contract-site
+/// <text>", ""()` naming the source location for diagnostics.
+///
+/// AMDGPUContractReport (MIR, after register allocation and before frame
+/// lowering) reports, for every expanded call, which registers stay live
+/// across it, and enforces "amdgpu-spill-policy"="error": any VGPR spill,
+/// stack object or more than "amdgpu-sgpr-lane-spill-max" SGPR lane spills is
+/// a compile error.
+//
+//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
+
